          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+classes"} Chern classes
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+bundles"} complex vector bundles
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+characteristic+classes"} universal characteristic classes
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+oriented+cohomology"} complex oriented
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+cohomology+theory"} generalized cohomology theory
            %em Conner-Floyd Chern classes
            (
            %a{:href => "#ConnerFloyd66"}> Conner-Floyd 66, Section 7
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Adams74"} Adams 74, Section I.4
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Kochman96"} Kochman 96, Section 4.3
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "#Lurie10"} Lurie 10, Lectures 4 and 5
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+cohomology+theory"} generalized cohomology theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+Chern+class"} first Chern class
            in
            = succeed "-cohomology" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+oriented+cohomology"} complex oriented cohomology
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/splitting+principle"} splitting principle
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "complex+oriented+cohomology+theory#TheCohomologyRingOfBUn"} complex oriented cohomology – the cohomology ring of BU(n)
          %p
            The Conner-Floyd Chern classes in top degree serve as the generalized
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+classes"} Thom classes
            that make every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+bundle"} complex vector bundle
            have
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation+in+generalized+cohomology"} orientation in generalized cohomology
            with respect to any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+oriented+cohomology+theory"} complex oriented cohomology theory
            (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie10"}> Lurie 10, lecture 5, prop. 6
            ).
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %p
            The definition of the
            = succeed "-Chern" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %a{:href => "#ConnerFloyd66"} Conner-Floyd 66, Theorem 7.6
            proceeds as follows.
          %p
            Let
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi c
                    %mn 1
                    %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_1^E
            in
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
